# enamel: enameled (magnet) wire (decision C21). The DIP in the vise legs
# up; the wire feeder feeds 40 mm of AWG 30 enameled wire; the rig bends
# its end 90 degrees, leaving a 4 mm end, which the arm lays alongside
# pin 3's leg (a lap joint, decision C22), the wire run along the pin
# row over pin 4, clear of it (where an enameled wire does touch a pin,
# its enamel insulates it). The iron at 400 C burns the enamel off only
# where it heats the wire, at the joint; pincer P2 bends the wire's other
# half down.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
lift A mm=60
wire S5 awg=30 mm=40 enamel=yes
pick A W1 grasp=middle
cut S5
lift A mm=60
insert A on=W1.1 at=14.5
form angle=90
lift A mm=60
bring A W1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=0,1,0 lap=3.2 from=0,0,1
pinch P1 on=W1.1 at=12
release A W1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+W1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+W1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+W1.1 dwell=3 temp=400
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+W1.1 below=100
scope aim=W1.2 zoom=3
bend P2 on=W1.2 at=6 angle=90 toward=0,0,-1
unpinch P1
inspect shorts
